  {
   "id": "401bbd83-1897-4b98-a54c-bf392545fd5b",
   "marks": 9,
   "state": "SUGGESTED",
   "qnum": null,
   "stem_len": 266,
   "stem": "The gas burned in a Bunsen burner is methane. The equation for the complete combustion of methane is $\\mathrm {C H} _ {4} (\\mathrm {g}) + 2 \\mathrm {O} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm {C O} _ {2} (\\mathrm {g}) + 2 \\mathrm {H} _ {2} \\mathrm {O} (\\mathrm {g})$"
  },
  {
   "id": "b4a2b62d-bcaa-4ef4-a334-c0460405f57c",
   "marks": 9,
   "state": "SUGGESTED",
   "qnum": null,
   "stem_len": 507,
   "stem": "A student uses this apparatus to investigate the temperature change that occurs when ammonium nitrate is dissolved in water. She uses this method. put $ 1 0 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of water into the polystyrene cup and measure the initial temperature of the water add 8.00 g of ammonium nitrate and stir record the lowest temperature reached by the solution The table shows her results. Initial temperat"
