  {
   "id": "1d1a881b-5d73-4d6c-8502-f2324060fa57",
   "marks": 14,
   "state": "SUGGESTED",
   "qnum": null,
   "stem_len": 494,
   "stem": "A salt can be made by reacting an acid with an insoluble base. The student uses this method. Stage 1 pour $ 5 0 \\mathrm{c m}^{3} $ of dilute sulfuric acid into a beaker Stage 2 warm the acid using a Bunsen burner Stage 3 add a small amount of copper(II) oxide to the warm acid and stir the mixture Stage 4 add further amounts of copper(II) oxide until copper(II) oxide is in excess Stage 5 filter the"
  },
  {
